From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:16:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(codex-native): bring web !command shell inputs up to its
 PR

When the bridge is idle, hold the injection lock until the forwarder records
the shell command's turn, so a follow-up message cannot double-start; keep a
trailing escaped space or heredoc body as part of the command; add the PR's
typed-!command e2e test. Matches the Codex part of
https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/11396. The Run button, its e2e
test and the claude-native shell test stay with run-suggested-commands.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Docs: none (fix: hardens the typed !command that docs/run-suggested-commands.md describes; no setting)
---
